--- a/pluggy/docs/index.rst
+++ b/pluggy/docs/index.rst
@@ -639,6 +639,38 @@
     pm.hook.myhook(config=config, args=args)
     # New caller; hookimpls will get new_arg="get this".
     pm.hook.myhook(config=config, args=args, new_arg="get this")
+
+
+.. _hookimpl_arg_default:
+
+Hookimpl argument defaults
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+A *hookimpl* may also declare a default value for an argument. The value the
+hookimpl receives for such an argument is, in order of precedence:
+
+1. the value passed by the hook call,
+2. the hookspec's :ref:`default value <hookspec_arg_default>`,
+3. the hookimpl's own default value.
+
+The hookimpl's default is therefore only used when neither the call nor the
+hookspec provides the argument, for example when a new hookimpl runs against
+an older hookspec which doesn't have the argument yet:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    @hookimpl
+    def myhook(config, args, new_arg="impl default"):
+        pass
+
+
+    # The hookimpl gets new_arg="get this".
+    pm.hook.myhook(config=config, args=args, new_arg="get this")
+
+This applies to plain hookimpls as well as to wrappers.
+
+.. versionchanged:: 1.7
+   Previously the hookimpl's default value was always used, even when the
+   hook call passed a value for the argument.
 
 
