 Repeating the option **replaces** the previous values (`--param a b --param c` becomes
 `['c']`), which is the opposite of `action=append`. `nargs='*'` is greedy: it consumes
 values until the next option flag, so a following subcommand name can be swallowed.
+
+A field is treated as a collection when its type is a subclass of `collections.abc.Sequence`,
+`collections.abc.Set` or `collections.abc.Mapping`, parameterized or bare, including inside `X | None`. Besides
+`list`, `set` and `dict` this covers e.g. `tuple`, `frozenset`, `deque`, `OrderedDict`, `MutableSequence` and
+`MutableMapping`. Such fields are repeated options (`--param a --param b`), can be wrapped in `CliVariadicArg`
+(also as `CliPositionalArg[CliVariadicArg[tuple[str, ...]]]`), and mapping subtypes take `key=value` arguments
+like `dict`. The parsed value has the field's own type. `str`, `bytes` and `bytearray` are sequences too, but
+always take a single value. Using `CliVariadicArg` on any other type raises a `SettingsError`
+(`CliVariadicArg requires a Sequence, Set, or Mapping type for <dest>`).
 
